  {
    "field_name": "Raw Output Example",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "sample_index,status,kernel,bandwidth_gb_s,peak_percent,runtime_ms,error_message\n0,ok,Copy,4200,79.2,1.0,"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Smoke Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --smoke --validate --device-id 0 --dtype FP64 --block-size 256 --array-size 1048576 --kernels Copy,Mul,Add,Triad,Dot --warmup-iters 1 --num-iterations 2 --output-format csv"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Baseline Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --baseline --validate --device-id 0 --dtype FP64 --block-size 256 --array-size 268435456 --kernels Copy,Mul,Add,Triad,Dot --warmup-iters 2 --num-iterations 30000 --output-format csv"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Extended Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --extended --validate --device-id 0 --dtype FP64 --block-size 256 --array-size 536870912 --kernels Copy,Mul,Add,Triad,Dot --warmup-iters 5 --num-iterations 40800 --output-format csv"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Output Fields / Metrics to Parse",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "kernel, bandwidth_gb_s, peak_percent, runtime_ms. Derived: bandwidth_gb_s_copy/mul/add/triad/dot and peak_percent_<kernel>. Blind means bandwidth_gb_s and peak_percent remain in summary.json but are no longer Metrics #1/#2"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Success Criteria",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Five kernel rows parse, each with a finite positive bandwidth_gb_s"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Parser and Normalization Notes",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "hip-stream already prints GB/s, so the collector does not divide by 1000. runtime_ms is the constant 1.0. peak_percent is min(100, bandwidth_gb_s/5300*100). parse_results.py keeps the cross-kernel mean and also writes bandwidth_gb_s_<kernel> for Copy, Mul, Add, Triad, and Dot"
  },
